  <prompt>Add the read-only MCP tool spaarke_list_playbooks: one list of the caller's playbooks (GET /api/ai/playbooks) and public playbooks (GET /api/ai/playbooks/public), de-duplicated by id, over IPlaybookService, run as the caller.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in MCP tool handlers and the JPS playbook service.</role>
  <goal>The tool returns exactly the union of the two REST lists for the same caller, with no duplicate ids, as slim rows (id, name, description ≤ 200 chars, owner kind, format).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-04, D-209 (qualify "playbook" by format). REST: Api/Ai/PlaybookEndpoints.cs (group /api/ai/playbooks; ListUserPlaybooks :90, ListPublicPlaybooks :98). The legacy de-duplication is readable at git show 37f0864afe:src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/AgentEndpoints.cs (:62, :334, :357).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Playbooks/ListPlaybooksTool.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Playbooks.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Playbooks/ListPlaybooksToolTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/PlaybookEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/CompleteDecisionTool.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">General McpToolResults, ledger partials</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Run as the caller (IHttpContextAccessor; UserContextRequired; no app-only fallback). Call the same IPlaybookService methods the two REST handlers call, with the same paging limits.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">[McpArea("legal-operations")], readOnlyHint true, destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true, a title, description ≤ 1,024 characters that says "JPS playbooks (AI analysis recipes)", not bare "playbook" (D-209). Ledger row in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Playbooks.cs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Slim rows only; no playbook definition JSON or prompts in model-visible text. Logs: tool name, latency, row count, outcome, correlation id. Result &lt; 64 KiB at the list maximum.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

